\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1\i\f0\fs22 Library Manager Cassandra Sargent announced a Bobblehead Painting for Teens program on Wednesday, March 18, 2026, from 4:00 PM to 5:00 PM.\line\line Waste Management Recycling Education Representative Bobby Bell announced a new update to plastic recycling: plastic No. 5 and paper to-go cups are now recyclable. He also reminded everyone to ensure containers are free of liquids and responded to City Council questions.\line\line Manhattan Beach resident Carol Patterson invited the community to attend the Manhattan Beach Community Church production of Fiddler on the Roof, which will open this weekend on Friday, March 20, 2026, and Saturday, March 21, 2026, at 7:30 PM.\line\line Eduardo Pech announced a community meeting for the 28\super th\nosupersub Street Storm Drain Infiltration Project, where staff will review the construction schedule, discuss anticipated impacts, and answer residents\rquote  questions. The meeting will be held at the Joslyn Community Center on March 19, 2026, from 7:30 PM to 8:30 PM.\line\line Mira Costa High School Band Teacher Joel Carlson invited the community to the Costa to the Capital fundraiser festival and send-off concert, taking place at the Mira Costa High School Auditorium on Friday, March 27, 2026, at 7:00 PM.\line\line Mira Costa High School student Samuel Rodriguez shared that he and his classmates have been working hard in band class, and that the experience has been a valuable educational opportunity. He noted their dedication and explained that they have been practicing as a team for the upcoming fundraiser and their visit to Washington, D.C.\line\line Mayor Lesser invited the community to attend Coffee with the Mayor at Metlox Plaza on Friday, April 3, 2026, from 9:00 AM to 10:00 AM. He also announced that this is the final meeting with Assistant City Clerk Martha Alvarez, thanked her for her dedication and ten years of service, and wished her well in her next chapter.\line\line City Manager Talyn Mirzakhanian and all members of the City Council also shared remarks in appreciation of Assistant City Clerk Alvarez.\cf1\i0\f1\par
